  "label": "Sheep-Like Conformity Stereotype",
  "description": "A cultural metaphor used to describe individuals or groups as blindly following orders or conforming without independent thought. The image of sheep showing their butts is commonly used in memes to imply this 'sheep-like' conformity or ignorance, which is a stereotype often applied to groups perceived as mindless or easily manipulated.",
